  "explanation": "The original sources present two distinct entities named POSB. Document D1S2 states that the 'Post Office Savings Bank (POSB)' was founded on January 1, 1877, in the Straits Settlements (now Singapore). Document D2S2 states that 'POSB was formed in 1904' as the 'Post Office Saving Bank,' which appears to be a separate entity in a different context. The addition of disambiguating qualifiers like '(Zimbabwean POSB)' clarifies the distinct referents while preserving the original claims. The other candidates (1999, 2001) refer to unrelated developments and are not relevant to the founding date."
